y each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =5\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id 17592186120422 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "767ebc71-0ad3-54b6-aa71-7c8c0b0f3bfc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438302} {:answer/id #uuid "a63f8938-30f5-513c-a258-cd4d1a6a7304" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "767ebc71-0ad3-54b6-aa71-7c8c0b0f3bfc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438302} :answer-field/id #uuid "57ffd47f-b693-5f52-b1f1-700e84eec01a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2809995c-d5a8-548e-8bde-0875034527de" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438304} {:answer/id #uuid "eaacdaf9-bb58-5783-b3f8-b3ace0a6d805" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaacdaf9-bb58-5783-b3f8-b3ace0a6d805" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438305} :answer-field/id #uuid "51bb348a-eb47-53be-9c6a-af21f5e21289" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439181} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ee6e55d-811b-5fea-8eb0-bfe2370d455c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438306} {:answer/id #uuid "26cce80e-998b-5997-9b94-fa52ef460fa0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26cce80e-998b-5997-9b94-fa52ef460fa0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438307} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8e98b2f-07d9-5dce-aec0-dbf12be54818" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "39d12d09-6555-5993-ad4c-5e191be1b0c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-42091" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** ${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $A$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${A}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186120426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119784 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76bc55da-83d7-5857-aa45-f67452354c98" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439761} {:answer/id #uuid "04de8af5-832b-52ca-a350-f0f854ef704b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76bc55da-83d7-5857-aa45-f67452354c98" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439761} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c2bf384-0f31-5769-a66a-ac9626e09eb9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186440238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae221432-f0bc-5791-a903-4cd7033afbd0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439763} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f39cf2-a8e6-5e3d-af10-2464a548d981" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1f39cf2-a8e6-5e3d-af10-2464a548d981" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439764} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b7c5ec-92af-5a70-b92f-f383dbb8df49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186440239} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d15953e8-d0a0-58aa-99b8-dbe3d3eb0376" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439765} {:answer/id #uuid "a57d22ef-51bd-5268-b831-4fd97df2edf1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186439766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d15953e8-d0a0-58aa-99b8-dbe3d3eb0376" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186439765} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d4fb36d-bf6c-5859-bad3-fc51a1c5bd9b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186440240}] :question/id #uuid "64e75667-2ca8-5517-b38f-4bfa5cf4e995" :question/math-academy-id "q-42115" :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A^{T} + A$ is upper triangular\n- **III.** $A$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "A is neither upper nor lower triangular because both off-diagonal entries a12=1 and a21=-1 are nonzero. However A^T+A=diag(-6,2,10), so statement II is true."}] [{:db/id 17592186120504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b19292e-d665-566f-8c6f-7d83c4d69c31" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186333545} {:answer/id #uuid "7039880d-285d-542d-8eed-1662170a86ab" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186334012} {:answer/id #uuid "7de24423-58a1-5fc2-baf5-dde65d746a91" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186334113} {:answer/id #uuid "ca309238-a2b3-5c28-8c7c-56e6c410616b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186334750} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe722d3-8558-53eb-8a6e-850293b2db44" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186335199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b19292e-d665-566f-8c6f-7d83c4d69c31" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186333545} :answer-field/id #uuid "96649b7c-8415-520e-af03-f8b52df45dd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186335522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c8b870-01b8-5cdd-a0e6-31fdbbd32f0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-68740" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id 17592186262602 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cec33d-a6da-5626-bbe2-b061760728e3" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id 17592186260607} {:answer/id #uuid "770ef76c-f319-50d7-8a97-d5c775bdeaac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186260915} {:answer/id #uuid "95a106ed-81ef-5c16-bdbc-d6be56d66200" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id 17592186261173} {:answer/id #uuid "a423decc-250a-5fd2-8836-863cae41272b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186261305} {:answer/id #uuid "a6349c37-feda-52d9-ab32-111b948babda" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id 17592186261320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "770ef76c-f319-50d7-8a97-d5c775bdeaac" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186260915} :answer-field/id #uuid "0596aab0-50de-5954-8cdb-1a2aeeaca5a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b95456b-3323-5d6f-9e68-2195aad3e714" :question/math-academy-id "q-126340" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${c}_{21}=-5\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id 17592186262603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "439d7166-1f7a-5882-84e5-7dddce5a67ce" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id 17592186260463} {:answer/id #uuid "81390c4d-a8fa-5c12-b430-1feedb8ec458" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186261000} {:answer/id #uuid "8fcf989e-ce46-55e5-aa4d-3df39