ow the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $B$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186269143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28741486-369e-5706-ae1b-b725c51b2ab6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186266505} {:answer/id #uuid "4e31dd9f-15de-59d3-94cd-966926a7e530" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186266840} {:answer/id #uuid "533fb3ba-63f1-555e-98ed-8058779ed29c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186266889} {:answer/id #uuid "b9bdd702-b2df-5c6c-a4c2-63341c07bd3f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186267810} {:answer/id #uuid "eadc47d2-6d03-54da-ac2e-565204378e46" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186268237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e31dd9f-15de-59d3-94cd-966926a7e530" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186266840} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbef8b98-e8a0-5930-88b8-fc4e670ab6d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186268740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f081148-4183-50c8-903b-3014f5de1d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-13760" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id 17592186269144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39aab90e-f541-501a-8b40-f432e91bddd0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186266652} {:answer/id #uuid "3a96214a-575e-53d6-9d07-a3b06bff410b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id 17592186266661} {:answer/id #uuid "690d4d65-e799-5ca4-aae2-bf9240fdb8bb" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id 17592186267077} {:answer/id #uuid "92ed2710-7671-5353-8733-329a0cb1dbd2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} 