& 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n\n- **III.** ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries above the main diagonal equal to zero: \n\n$$\n{A}^{T}+A=\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186269148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb812af-4792-5005-bf12-c4f311aa7f5f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id 17592186266422} {:answer/id #uuid "39133468-8ed3-59ca-8b82-06709d2e55a7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186266641} {:answer/id #uuid "5e319411-851a-5336-ad88-c3bb29d2473a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id 17592186266976} {:answer/id #uuid "83eda5b8-676e-5cc5-a9a9-f531883a6c28" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id 17592186267305} {:answer/id #uuid "91fdf0d1-ee68-5239-857e-a5863bc6e9b8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186267443}] :answer-fie