e" :db/id 17592186438513} :answer-field/id #uuid "716e9941-8550-5bde-a973-86bb302cfd14" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10915988-162b-5dec-9de2-5241d5fc3202" :question/math-academy-id "q-74319" :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $D$ is upper triangular\n\n- **II.** $D$ is lower triangular\n\n- **III.** ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular" :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $D$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $D$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${D}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186396038 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3993775-0f8e-5c7e-b158-1a52fe75de99" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id 17592186396040} {:answer/id #uuid "d4aa5d0b-3502-5db7-982d-257ca9d0ebb8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id 17592186396041} {:answer/id #uuid "9c6da7fb-8eba-5ffa-9bde-d1144a8dbb47" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186396042} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc5b9ce-5da0-55fe-8e2a-df8eb4ecfc52" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Diagonal matrix" :db/id 17592186396043} {:answer/id #uuid "6657fbe8-1958-5cc4-b147-eb6c679992c6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186396044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6657fbe8-1958-5cc4-b147-eb6c679992c6" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Upper triangular matrix" :db/id 17592186396044} :answer-field/id #uuid "2332d85e-5e88-505c-b823-5f0ae7f57fb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186396039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ce57af24-7688-5285-99c2-a982d174d89c" :question/math-academy-id "q-13781" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=4\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id 17592186398284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2542e69d-df39-5c64-b554-6be1595617c7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398286} {:answer/id #uuid "f60fef53-a0d6-5dc0-ab21-ab9df9058607" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398287} {:answer/id #uuid "cae5bb2d-1f92-5e20-ba17-23b594a7c310" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398288} {:answer/id #uuid "25367444-9d31-5d08-911d-e0197f9f8855" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398289} {:answer/id #uuid "dcecc6d5-1e1c-5114-8664-36c7f108f7a5" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25367444-9d31-5d08-911d-e0197f9f8855" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398289} :answer-field/id #uuid "0957fc2a-fd8b-5808-9041-6cd8fd6371ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186398285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c5c71ff-a77d-5a86-8573-305cd57f3d0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126353" :question/problem "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id 17592186398975 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d64405d0-289f-509a-b6c2-4ddc819a550c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398977} {:answer/id #uuid "21195042-f7c2-5911-a358-864f5699c6dd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398978} {:answer/id #uuid "daa40cbf-4d3b-590b-81d0-b66a0577167e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398979} {:answer/id #uuid "4b82a1dd-a8a6-5b78-82c9-fa1f39c4845b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398980} {:answer/id #uuid "7585a86b-d9f0-55bc-8e6f-efb92e7d43c2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7585a86b-d9f0-55bc-8e6f-efb92e7d43c2" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id 17592186398981} :answer-field/id #uuid "29184956-f54b-5670-ad89-7254d448c06c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186398976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9af406e1-4ead-558e-9219-f0bb53a377fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74316" :question/problem "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices."}] [{:db/id 17592186479911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "296f59f7-109c-5bb3-a36b-3539d82489f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186479919} {:answer/id #uuid "60727414-e86c-54e5-9531-2ea37c5e4ce7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186479924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "296f59f7-109c-5bb3-a36b-3539d82489f9" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186479919} :answer-field/id #uuid "043d5cd6-05d5-59e0-9ca8-06fddfd63945" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186479908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a560e13-60b8-571c-bb17-a2dcbf607b21" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186479920} {:answer/id #uuid "da1c2f09-76f7-56ff-9174-0a1697e466a7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/va